---
layout: base.njk
title: Home
description: Joseph Chazalon — computer vision, NLP, and machine learning for document understanding, historical sources, and reproducible evaluation.
bodyClass: is-home
---
<div class="home-layout">
  <div class="home-main">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p class="lede">Assistant Professor in Computer Science (PhD), <a href="http://www.epita.fr/">EPITA</a> Research Lab. (<a href="https://www.lre.epita.fr/">LRE</a>), Le Kremlin-Bicêtre, France. I work on computer vision, machine learning, and NLP applied to document analysis—especially historical documents—with emphasis on evaluation protocols and reproducible research.</p>

    <p class="home-actions">
      {% if site.cvUrl %}<a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ site.cvUrl }}">CV / résumé (PDF)</a>{% endif %}
      {% if site.scheduleUrl %}<a class="btn" href="{{ site.scheduleUrl }}">Book an appointment</a>{% endif %}
      <a class="btn" href="{{ '/contact/' | url }}">Contact &amp; opportunities</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Research topics</h2>
    <ul class="compact-list">
      <li><strong>Core:</strong> document image analysis and indexing; text extraction and downstream NLP from noisy OCR in historical material; linking data across sources for structured outputs useful to the social sciences and humanities</li>
      <li><strong>Broader applications:</strong> face analysis, document fraud detection, medical imaging—when projects call for it</li>
      <li><strong>Practice:</strong> collaborative projects, datasets, competitions (e.g. ICDAR), open-source prototypes, and evaluation frameworks researchers can actually use</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Profiles</h2>
    <p class="profiles-inline">
      <a href="https://github.com/jchazalon/">GitHub</a> ·
      <a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3757-074X">ORCID</a> ·
      <a href="https://scholar.google.fr/citations?user=zu8wSDAAAAAJ">Google Scholar</a> ·
      <a href="https://dblp.org/pers/hd/c/Chazalon:Joseph">DBLP</a> ·
      <a href="https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/search/index/?qa[authIdHal_s][]=joseph-chazalon">HAL</a> ·
      <a href="https://www.idref.fr/171616030">IdRef</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Biography (short)</h2>
    <p>I hold an engineering degree (2008) and a Ph.D. (2013) in Computer Science from <a href="https://www.insa-rennes.fr/">INSA Rennes</a> (thesis: interactive analysis of 18th-century register images). I was a research engineer at the <a href="https://l3i.univ-larochelle.fr/">L3i</a>, University of La Rochelle (2013–2018), then joined <a href="https://www.lre.epita.fr/">EPITA–LRE</a> as an assistant professor (2018–present). I have taught 1,200+ hours from undergraduate to master’s level (computer vision, machine learning, GPU programming, DevOps, and related topics). I am an active member of IAPR TC11 (“Reading Systems”) and coordinate or contribute to several collaborative projects—see <a href="{{ '/projects/' | url }}">Projects</a> and <a href="{{ '/publications/' | url }}">Publications</a>.{% if site.cvUrl %} A PDF résumé is available: <a href="{{ site.cvUrl }}">CV / résumé</a>.{% endif %}</p>
  </div>

  {% set recentBlog = collections.posts | recentBlogPosts(4) %}
  <aside class="home-aside" aria-label="News and recent blog posts">
    <h2 class="home-aside-title">News</h2>
    <ul class="news-compact">
      {% for item in news | sortNews %}
      {% if loop.index <= 8 %}
      <li>
        <time datetime="{{ item.date }}">{{ item.date }}</time>
        <a href="{{ '/news/' | url }}#news-{{ item.date }}">{{ item.summary | default(item.title) }}</a>
      </li>
      {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="home-aside-more"><a href="{{ '/news/' | url }}">All news →</a></p>

    {% if recentBlog.length %}
    <h2 class="home-aside-title home-aside-title--sub">Blog</h2>
    <ul class="news-compact">
      {% for post in recentBlog %}
      <li>
        <time datetime="{{ post.date | isoDate }}">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</time>
        <a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="home-aside-more"><a href="{{ '/blog/' | url }}">All posts →</a></p>
    {% endif %}
  </aside>
</div>
